  "what_this_is": "Cell B0r (docs/readiness/2026-09-17-slurp-b0-replicate-v1-preregistration.md): the same-roster OWN-NULL REPLICATE of cell B0, the review-off ablation configs/baseline/slurp-native-dual-store-train-fold-a-review-off-v1.json. Not one configured channel moves: the same arm, policy phase-native-candidates-solve-v1, the same native episode role graph (Reviewer and Planner at max_iterations 0, max_revisions 0), the same model fragment (temperature 0, seed 20260913, max_tokens 512), the same dataset fragment and 1,080-row TRAIN Fold A roster, the same two knowledge stores with their release and snapshot hashes, the same candidate supply contract, the same phase material and instruction templates, the same inert phase_tools block, the same promoted speech packets, the same resident geometry and the same speech-feature identity strings as B0 -- those identity strings are held at B0's values on purpose, because a replicate that renamed them would not be a replicate; they are provenance only (core.model.transport validates and drops them; they never enter the rendered messages), and fit receipts are namespaced by the FIT run and attempt id, so holding them cannot collide. Only the run, attempt and native-fit identities are fresh, and the prepared first-phase supply is rebuilt because core.preparation.artifact_inputs binds the composed values (run and attempt ids included) and the rails/core module digests, both of which moved since B0 flew at 5d0d694d. The factor under test is therefore batch composition under greedy decoding on this runtime and nothing else: llama-server at temperature 0 does not return bytes independent of how requests batch across slots, so a cell that changes nothing still moves the numbers, and the size of that movement is the SLURP TRAIN Fold A own-null half-width the B0 re-decision needs. Fold B is absent. The separate generation and native fit identities do not authorize contact; readiness is held until the coordinator adds the decision receipt and flips it.",
